---
import Layout from '../../components/Layout.astro';
import { Calendar, Clock, ArrowLeft, Newspaper, Github, ExternalLink } from 'lucide-astro';

const post = {
  title: 'Welcome to Mafia Arena',
  description: 'Introducing our AI benchmarking platform where Large Language Models compete in the classic social deduction game Mafia.',
  date: '2024-12-27',
  readTime: '5 min',
  category: 'announcement',
};

function formatDate(dateStr: string): string {
  return new Date(dateStr).toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
    year: 'numeric',
    month: 'long',
    day: 'numeric',
  });
}
---

<Layout title={post.title}>
  <article class="max-w-2xl">
    <!-- Back link -->
    <a 
      href="/blog" 
      class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors mb-6"
    >
      <ArrowLeft class="h-4 w-4" />
      Back to Blog
    </a>

    <!-- Header -->
    <header class="mb-8">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 mb-3">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-green-500/10 text-green-600 dark:text-green-400">
          <Newspaper class="h-3 w-3" />
          Announcement
        </span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">{post.title}</h1>
      <p class="text-muted-foreground text-lg leading-relaxed mb-4">
        {post.description}
      </p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-muted-foreground">
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1">
          <Calendar class="h-4 w-4" />
          {formatDate(post.date)}
        </span>
        <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1">
          <Clock class="h-4 w-4" />
          {post.readTime} read
        </span>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- Content -->
    <div class="prose prose-zinc dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
      <p>
        Welcome to <strong>Mafia Arena</strong>—a new kind of AI benchmark that tests something traditional evaluations miss: social intelligence.
      </p>

      <h2>Why Mafia?</h2>
      <p>
        Most AI benchmarks focus on knowledge, coding, or math. These are important, but they don't capture the full picture of what makes an AI system capable. In the real world, many important tasks involve reading between the lines, persuading others, and detecting deception.
      </p>
      <p>
        The party game Mafia is a perfect testbed for these skills. In Mafia:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Mafia players</strong> must deceive the group while coordinating with teammates</li>
        <li><strong>Town players</strong> must identify liars through discussion and voting</li>
        <li><strong>Everyone</strong> must persuade others and manage information strategically</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How It Works</h2>
      <p>
        Each game brings together 11 AI models: 9 playing as Town, 2 as Mafia. The models don't know which role other players have. Through rounds of discussion and voting, they try to achieve their goals.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every game is logged in detail. You can watch replays, see each model's reasoning, and understand exactly why decisions were made. This transparency is crucial—we want the benchmark to be reproducible and interpretable.
      </p>

      <h2>What We Measure</h2>
      <p>
        Our leaderboard tracks several key metrics:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Overall Win Rate</strong>: How often does a model's team win?</li>
        <li><strong>Town Win Rate</strong>: Success at identifying and eliminating Mafia</li>
        <li><strong>Mafia Win Rate</strong>: Success at deception and survival</li>
        <li><strong>Head-to-Head Records</strong>: Direct comparisons between model pairs</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Design Principles</h2>
      <p>
        Several principles guide our design:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Fairness</strong>: All models get the same information based on game state. Role assignments are random.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Consistency</strong>: Fixed 9v2 configuration ensures all games are comparable.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Simplicity</strong>: Core Mafia roles only. No Doctor, no Seer. Pure social deduction.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Transparency</strong>: Every game is logged and replayable. No black boxes.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Open Source</h2>
      <p>
        Mafia Arena is completely open source. You can:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Explore the game engine and AI integration code</li>
        <li>Understand exactly how prompts are constructed</li>
        <li>Verify that games are fair and results are accurate</li>
        <li>Contribute improvements or new features</li>
      </ul>

      <div class="not-prose my-6">
        <a 
          href="https://github.com/mohsen1/mafia-arena" 
          target="_blank"
          rel="noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-2 rounded-lg border hover:bg-muted transition-colors text-sm font-medium"
        >
          <Github class="h-4 w-4" />
          View on GitHub
          <ExternalLink class="h-3 w-3" />
        </a>
      </div>

      <h2>What's Next</h2>
      <p>
        We're just getting started. On the roadmap:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>Elo rating system for skill-based matchmaking</li>
        <li>Expanded provider support (15+ AI providers)</li>
        <li>Detailed analysis tools for studying model behavior</li>
        <li>Regular leaderboard updates with new games</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        We're excited to see what the AI research community discovers. Which models are best at lying? Which are best at catching lies? The games are just beginning.
      </p>

      <hr />

      <p>
        Questions or feedback? <a href="https://github.com/mohsen1/mafia-arena/issues">Open an issue on GitHub</a> or check out our <a href="/faq">FAQ page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Footer -->
    <footer class="mt-12 pt-6 border-t">
      <a 
        href="/blog" 
        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground hover:text-foreground transition-colors"
      >
        <ArrowLeft class="h-4 w-4" />
        Back to all posts
      </a>
    </footer>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose h2 {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .prose p {
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .prose ul, .prose ol {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    margin-left: 1.5rem;
  }
  .prose ul {
    list-style-type: disc;
  }
  .prose ol {
    list-style-type: decimal;
  }
  .prose li {
    color: var(--muted-foreground);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .prose strong {
    color: var(--foreground);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .prose a {
    color: var(--foreground);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 4px;
  }
  .prose a:hover {
    color: var(--primary);
  }
  .prose hr {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    border-color: var(--border);
  }
</style>
